# Core systems

Full guide: [docs/SYSTEMS.md](../../docs/SYSTEMS.md) · Framework: [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](../../docs/ARCHITECTURE.md)

## Lifecycle

```text
Constructor → ISavable.Load() (all systems) → IInitializable.Initialize() (bind order)
```

```csharp
void ISavable.Load()
{
    var save = SaveLoadStorage.Load<MySave>(SAVE_KEY);
    foreach (var asset in _config.AssetCollection)
    {
        // merge save → new ItemRuntime(asset, ...)
    }
}

public void Initialize()
{
    _otherSystem.OnEvent += Handler; // not in Load()
}
```

## Layers (collection-based)

| Layer | Example |
|-------|---------|
| Config | `CurrencyConfig` : `BaseConfig` |
| Item asset | `CurrencyItemAsset` : `BaseItemAsset` |
| Item runtime | `CurrencyItemRuntime` + `AmountProperty` |
| Item save | `CurrencyItemSave` in `CurrencySave` |

## Mutations and dirty save

After **any** change to persisted runtime state, call `OnSaveRequired?.Invoke()`.  
`SaveLoadService` marks the savable **dirty**; `ExecuteSaves()` (app pause/quit, Core shutdown) calls `ISavable.Save()` only for dirty systems.

Do **not** call `SaveLoadStorage.Save` from gameplay code.

```csharp
public void AddAmount(string identifier, int amount)
{
    var itemRuntime = GetItemRuntime(identifier);

    itemRuntime.Amount.AddValue(amount);
    OnSaveRequired?.Invoke();
}
```

Every public mutator that changes saved data must end with `OnSaveRequired?.Invoke()` (add, remove, unlock, level up, etc.).

UI reads **Runtime**, never save DTOs.
